  "evidence": "The list callbacks registered in todolist-043.json retrieve a row index via 0xc588310. Checkbox callback passes it with the current list state to 0xc680490; two row callbacks pass it in navigation data to detail or sub-list. Sub-list callback retrieves the index, directly addresses a 12-byte subitem record, updates its state and reorders records. List row builder invokes the title, progress, repeat and time helpers from both row creation and update paths.",
  "scope": "Individual event-data getters and UI setter call sites; row helpers may fire repeatedly for different tasks. Formatted time through the separate variadic text function is not included.",
  "limitations": "The sub-list callback uses the returned index without a local bounds check and may write task state. Replacing indices can target another item, corrupt memory or trigger invalid accesses. Slots do not guarantee thread quiescence; device behavior and recovery are unverified. Avoid recording task contents.",
